Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 9 Windows Application Control Fault

@ [fault_record_uuid] 0776dd05-8cad-459f-8453-a80e48af8d29
@ [occurred_at] 2026-08-20
@ [scope] immutable_native_lifecycle_custody_focused_release_execution

& [Observation]
  + the focused native debug harness passed all twenty-six tests
  + native warnings-denied focused Clippy passed
  + Windows compiled the focused optimized release harness but refused to launch the newly emitted executable with operating-system error 4551
  + no optimized assertion ran in that refused Windows process

& [Classification]
  + the refusal is a host Application Control decision over a fresh executable identity rather than a failed Cantor assertion
  + successful native debug evidence remains valid but cannot substitute for native optimized execution

& [ResolutionEvidence]
  + Ubuntu-24.04 WSL2 used isolated CARGO_TARGET_DIR /tmp/cantor-slice9-target and locked offline dependencies
  + focused debug and overflow-checked optimized release each passed twenty-six tests
  + complete debug and overflow-checked optimized workspace gates each registered 909 tests passed 908 failed zero and retained one governed ignore
  + workspace all-target all-feature warnings-denied Clippy passed

& [Security]
  + Smart App Control Code Integrity signer trust and host policy were not disabled weakened bypassed or reconfigured
  + no alternate executable was represented as Windows-native optimized execution
